"COMPLETE SETS: General Orders, LBR; LBR Forms; TCG Supplements | Central District of California | United States Bankruptcy Court (https://www.cacb.uscourts.gov/the-central-guide/complete-sets-general-orders-lbr-lbr-forms-tcg-supplements)\nciteturn1215view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"turn1212view1\",\"lineno\":25}); Total lines: 118\nL0: cite0†Skip to main content L1: \nL2: # cite1†United States Bankruptcy Court L3: \nL4: ## cite1†Central District of California L5: \nL6: # cite1†Hon. Julia W. Brand, Chief Judge • Kathleen J. Campbell, Clerk of Court L7: \nL8: ## Search form\nL9: \nL10: Search this site [Input: Enter search words]\nL11: \nL12: [Input]\nL13: \nL14: [Input] [Input]\nL15: \nL16: ## You are here\nL17: # COMPLETE SETS: General Orders, LBR; LBR Forms; TCG Supplements\nL18: \nL19: Search this site [Input: Search The Central Guide]\nL20: \nL21: [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input]\nL22: \nL23: [Input]\nL24: \nL25: cite2†Section 1 - Common Bankruptcy Procedures & Information L26: \nL27: cite3†Section 2 - Serving Documents & Giving Notice L28: \nL29: cite4†Section 3 - Judges' Procedures -- Judges' Webpages L30: \nL31: cite5†Section 4 - Match Local Bankruptcy Rules with Forms L32: \nL33: 1000:  COMPLETE SETS of LBR. LBR Forms, TCG Supplements, General Orders, Public Notices\nL34: \"Complete Set of LBR\" means you will find all Local Bankruptcy Rules in numerical sequence, from LBR 1001-1 to LBR 9075-1.  Note that every LBR has a \"dash\" in the number, such as 9075-1.  See link below.\nL35:   * The remainder of LBR listed in The Central Guide are individual LBR or subsections of a LBR\nL36:   * Note that a LBR applies to all bankruptcy chapters unless the rule limits its application to only a specific chapter, such as chapter 11 or 13.\nL37:   * Some rules listed in Section 4 of The Central Guide do not contain a dash.  These are FRBP instead of LBR.\nL38: \"Complete Set of LBR Forms\" means you will find all Local Bankruptcy Rules Forms in numerical and alphabetical sequence, starting with forms related to LBR 1002-1 to LBR 9075-1.  See link below\nL39:   * The remainder of LBR forms listed in the Central Guide are matched with the specific LBR that is related to that LBR form.\nL40:   * Note that a few forms apply only to a specific chapter in bankruptcy.  If so, the chapter number will be included in the form.  Otherwise, if there is no chapter number listed in the caption of a form, that form can be used in more than one chapter type.\nL41: \"Complete Set of TCG Supplements\" means you will find all 20 TCG Supplements in numerical order based on the number of the related FRBP Rule or LBR Rule.\nL42: \nL43: \"General Orders\" is a link to all orders that apply to all parties district wide; general orders can be entered in emergency situations or when it is clear the situation may change and the order process requires flexibility.  See link below\nL44: \"Public Notices\" is a link to notices that are posted several times each year to apprise the public of new or amended LBR, LBR Forms, and General Orders.  In addition, a Public Notice may identity dates when the court is closed.  See link below.\nL45: \nL46: \"Complete Set of FRBP\" means you will find a link to a database of all Federal Rules of Bankruptcy Procedure.\nL47: \"Complete Set of FRCP\" means you will find a link to a database of all Federal Rules of Civil Procedure.  Many of the FRCP apply in bankruptcy cases.  When this is true, a FRBP rule will indicate that a related FRCP rule applies.\nL48: \nL49: \nL50: \nL51: Section:\nL52: \nL53: Section 4 - Match Local Bankruptcy Rules with Forms\nL54: \nL55: Section Number or LBR Number:\nL56: \nL57: 1000\nL58: \nL59: Reference to Common Topics:\nL60: \nL61: cite6†Rules & Procedures L62: \nL63: Reference to Common Links:\nL64: \nL65: cite7†General Orders -- Complete Set L66: \nL67: cite8†Local Bankruptcy Rules -- Complete Set L68: cite9†LBR Edits -- Redline -- Public Comment Period L69: \nL70: cite10†Local Bankruptcy Rule Forms -- Complete Set L71: \nL72: cite11†Public Notices L73: \nL74: cite12†Federal Rules of Bankruptcy Procedure -- Complete Set†www.federalrulesofbankruptcyprocedure.org L75: \nL76: cite13†Federal Rules of Civil Procedure -- Complete Set†www.federalrulesofcivilprocedure.org L77: \nL78: cite14†Bankruptcy Code -- All Chapters†uscode.house.gov L79: \nL80: cite15†TCG Supplement 1002-1(c): Checklists of Forms to File a Bankruptcy Case L81: \nL82: cite16†TCG Supplement 1002-1(d): Privacy Policy L83: cite17†TCG Supplement 1007-1: Master Mailing List L84: \nL85: cite18†TCG Supplement 1071-1(a)(1): ZIP Codes to Determine Proper Division for Filing a Bankruptcy Case L86: \nL87: cite19†TCG Supplement 1071-1(a)(2): Phone Directory for Clerks Office and Chambers L88: \nL89: cite20†TCG Supplement 2002-2(a): United States Trustee; 341(a) Meeting Locations L90: \nL91: cite21†TCG Supplement 3007-1: Objections to Claims L92: \nL93: cite22†TCG Supplement 3015-1: Chapter 13, Presumptively Reasonable Supplemental Fees L94: cite23†TCG Supplement 5003(a)-(b)): Viewing Electronic Dockets; Archives L95: \nL96: cite24†TCG Supplement 5003(e): Addresses of Federal & State Agencies L97: \nL98: cite25†TCG Supplement 5005-2(d): Serving a Judge's Copy L99: \nL100: cite26†TCG Supplement 5005-4: CM/ECF Procedures L101: \nL102: cite27†TCG Supplement 5010-1: Table of Fees When Filing a Motion to Reopen a Bankruptcy Case L103: \nL104: cite28†TCG Supplement 5075-1: Mega Case Procedures L105: \nL106: cite29†TCG Supplement 7054-1: Bill of Costs L107: cite30†TCG Supplement 9004-1: Form and Format of Documents to be Filed, Lodged, or Served L108: \nL109: cite31†TCG Supplement 9006: Three Additional Days to Act or Respond L110: \nL111: cite32†TCG Supplement 9021-1: Lodged Order Upload Procedures (LOU) L112: \nL113: cite33†TCG Supplement 9021-1(c)(7): Orders that the Clerk Has Authority to Sign L114: \nL115: cite34†TCG Supplement 9075-1: Emergency Contacts for Judge's Chambers L116: \nL117: Your browser does not support Javascript. Your browser does not support Javascript.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n (https://cdn.ca9.uscourts.gov/datastore/bap/2015/02/02/GENORD_cmecf_Feb_2015.pdf)\nciteturn1215view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 days ago; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 7; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn1212view2\",\"id\":13}); Total lines: 189\nL0@P0: United States Bankruptcy Appellate Panel\nL1@P0: for the Ninth Circuit\nL2@P0: Administrative Order Regarding Electronic Filing in\nL3@P0: BAP Cases\nL4@P0: [February 2, 2015]\nL5@P0: The United States Bankruptcy Appellate Panel for the Ninth Circuit (“BAP”)\nL6@P0: adopts the following provisions to govern the electronic filing of documents in\nL7@P0: cases before the BAP. These provisions may be amended from time to time, with\nL8@P0: or without prior notice, by further order of the BAP. The BAP may deviate from\nL9@P0: these procedures in specific cases if deemed appropriate in the exercise of its\nL10@P0: discretion.\nL11@P0: Questions concerning electronic filing should be directed to the Clerk's\nL12@P0: office at 626-229-7220 or 626-229-7225, or can be emailed to:\nL13@P0: cmecf_bapca9@ca9.uscourts.gov\nL14@P0: Rule 1 - Electronic Registration and Filing Mandatory for Attorneys\nL15@P0: (a) Unless the BAP grants a request to be exempted from these requirements,\nL16@P0: (1) all attorneys appearing, participating, or wanting to receive notices in\nL17@P0: appeals before the BAP must register with the BAP’s Case\nL18@P0: Management/Electronic Case Filing (CM/ECF) docketing system; and\nL19@P0: (2) electronic filing using the BAP’s CM/ECF docketing system is\nL20@P0: mandatory for all attorneys.\nL21@P0: (b) An attorney who seeks exemption from the requirement of mandatory\nL22@P0: electronic filing may file a motion which states the reasons why the attorney\nL23@P0: should be exempted from electronic filing. The BAP Clerk shall have the\nL24@P0: authority to grant or deny such motions.\nL25@P0: Rule 2 - Registration and Training\nL26@P0: (a) Registration is required to obtain a login and password for use of CM/ECF.\nL27@P0-1: 1(b) Registration is required specifically for the BAP, and this registration is\nL28@P1: separate from registration for PACER or ECF in other courts.\nL29@P1: (c) Licensed attorneys authorized to practice before the BAP may register\nL30@P1: without leave of court at:\nL31@P1: www.pacer.gov\nL32@P1: (d) Any litigant who is not a licensed attorney authorized to practice before the\nL33@P1: BAP may file a motion requesting leave to register for CM/ECF.\nL34@P1: (e) The Ninth Circuit Court of Appeals has computer-based training modules\nL35@P1: explaining CM/ECF, PACER reports, and electronic filing. These training\nL36@P1: modules can be accessed by logging into the court of appeals website\nL37@P1: (www.ca9.uscourts.gov) and selecting “Electronic Filing - CM/ECF”. The\nL38@P1: BAP strongly encourages all filers to review these training materials, as the\nL39@P1: BAP’s electronic filing system is very similar to that of the court of appeals.\nL40@P1: Rule 3 - Excerpts of Record\nL41@P1: (a) Excerpts of Record. For all cases opened at the BAP beginning February 1,\nL42@P1: 2015, all excerpts of record must be filed electronically.\nL43@P1: (1) A table of contents must be included in a separate .pdf which is the\nL44@P1: first attachment to the excerpts of record docket event. Each\nL45@P1: subsequent item in the excerpts of record must be contained in a\nL46@P1: separate .pdf and labeled so that it is identifiable from the table of\nL47@P1: contents. Every effort should be made to attach all .pdf’s to the same\nL48@P1: docket event.\nL49@P1: (b) Excerpts of Record. For cases opened before February 1, 2015, electronic\nL50@P1: filing of the excerpts of record is optional. If excerpts are filed\nL51@P1: electronically, no paper copies are required. If excerpts are not filed\nL52@P1: electronically, the form, content and number of paper copies of a party’s\nL53@P1: excerpts of record must continue to comply with the requirements of\nL54@P1: Federal Rule of Bankruptcy Procedure 8018 and Ninth Circuit BAP Rule\nL55@P1: 8018(b)-1.\nL56@P1: (c) Service. All parties must serve a paper copy of the excerpts of record on any\nL57@P1: party not registered for BAP cm/ecf on the same day the excerpts of record\nL58@P1-2: 2are electronically filed.\nL59@P2: Rule 4 - Documents Which Can Not Be Filed Electronically\nL60@P2: (a) Sealed Documents & Motions to File Documents Under Seal. Sealed\nL61@P2: documents must be filed in paper format and must be accompanied by an\nL62@P2: electronic version of the document on either CD or DVD. This includes\nL63@P2: motions for permission to file a document under seal. The motion should\nL64@P2: state whether the filing party believes the motion to seal itself may be made\nL65@P2: available to the public or should remain sealed.\nL66@P2: Rule 5 - Signature\nL67@P2: (a) All electronic filings must be signed.\nL68@P2: (b) A signature consists of an \"/s/\" immediately followed by the typed name of\nL69@P2: each signatory, or by some substantially similar method effectively\nL70@P2: demonstrating the signatory’s intent to sign the filing.\nL71@P2: Rule 6 - Service\nL72@P2: (a) A Certificate of Service is required for all electronic filings, and filers must\nL73@P2: comply with the provisions of Federal Rule of Bankruptcy Procedure\nL74@P2: 8011(b), (c) and (d) when filing electronically.\nL75@P2: (b) Sample Certificates of Service for documents electronically filed are\nL76@P2: attached to this Order.\nL77@P2: (c) The CM/ECF system will generate a Notice of Docket Activity when any\nL78@P2: document is electronically filed. This notice constitutes service of the\nL79@P2: document on all parties who have registered as BAP electronic filers\nL80@P2: pursuant to Rule 2, above. Such registration constitutes consent to service\nL81@P2: via the Notice of Docket Activity.\nL82@P2: (I) A filing party may obtain the names and addresses of parties who\nL83@P2: have not registered for BAP electronic filing by logging into\nL84@P2: CM/ECF, then selecting “Reports”, then selecting “Service List”, and\nL85@P2: then typing in the case number.\nL86@P2: (ii) A filing party is not required to serve a paper copy of any\nL87@P2-3: 3electronically-filed document on any party who has registered as a\nL88@P3: BAP electronic filer.\nL89@P3: (iii) Except as provided in the BAP’s fax filing rule (9th Cir. BAP Rule\nL90@P3: 8011(a)-2), or unless otherwise agreed in writing between the parties,\nL91@P3: a filing party must serve a paper copy of any electronically-filed\nL92@P3: document on any party who has not registered as a BAP electronic\nL93@P3: filer, and must comply with Federal Rule of Bankruptcy Procedure\nL94@P3: 8011 (b), (c) and (d).\nL95@P3: (iv) Unless otherwise ordered, a Notice of Docket Activity generated after\nL96@P3: close of business (5:00 p.m. Pacific Time), or on a weekend or holiday\nL97@P3: will be deemed served on all registered BAP electronic filers at the\nL98@P3: start of the next business day.\nL99@P3: (d) For any document filed in paper format, the filer must comply with Federal\nL100@P3: Rule of Bankruptcy Procedure 8011 (b), (c) and (d).\nL101@P3: Rule 7 - Filing Deadlines\nL102@P3: (a) Electronic filing is permitted at all times, except when the system is\nL103@P3: temporarily unavailable due to routine or emergency maintenance.\nL104@P3: (b) Unless otherwise ordered, an electronic filing will be considered filed as of\nL105@P3: the date and time the filing is successfully completed. The BAP's CM/ECF\nL106@P3: system determines the date and time a filing is completed. A filing is timely\nL107@P3: only if it is accomplished in accordance with the deadlines set by all\nL108@P3: applicable court notices, orders, rules and statutes.\nL109@P3: (c) If a technical failure prevents timely electronic filing of any document, the\nL110@P3: filing party should promptly seek relief from the BAP.\nL111@P3: Rule 8 - Technical Requirements\nL112@P3: (a) All electronic filings must be in Portable Document Format (also known as\nL113@P3: .pdf or Adobe Acrobat Format).\nL114@P3: (b) Except as otherwise specified in this Rule, or as otherwise ordered, the text\nL115@P3: of all electronic filings must be searchable using Adobe Acrobat’s text\nL116@P3: search function.\nL117@P3-4: 4(c) For some documents, primarily exhibits, a text-searchable version might not\nL118@P4: be available. If so, the electronic filer may upload a version that is not text\nL119@P4: searchable.\nL120@P4: (d) Until further notice, the maximum size for a single attachment is 50\nL121@P4: megabytes. Attachments exceeding 50 megabytes must be divided into\nL122@P4: multiple attachments.\nL123@P4: Rule 9 - Hyperlinks\nL124@P4: (a) Electronic filings may contain hyperlinks to statutes, rules, regulations, and\nL125@P4: opinions.\nL126@P4: (b) Hyperlinks do not replace citations to the appendix, record, or legal\nL127@P4: authority. Documents must contain standard citations in support of\nL128@P4: statements of fact or points of law, in addition to any hyperlink. Hyperlinks\nL129@P4: are simply mechanisms for accessing material cited in a filed document and\nL130@P4: are not considered part of the appellate record. The BAP accepts no\nL131@P4: responsibility for the availability or functionality of any hyperlink and does\nL132@P4: not endorse any organization, product, or content at any hyperlinked site.\nL133@P4: Rule 10 - Privacy\nL134@P4: (a) In compliance with Fed. R. App. P. 25(a)(5) and Fed. R. Bankr. P. 9037,\nL135@P4: parties must refrain from including, or must partially redact where inclusion\nL136@P4: is necessary, the following personal data identifiers from all documents filed\nL137@P4: with the BAP:\nL138@P4: < Minors' names (use initials only);\nL139@P4: < Social Security numbers (use last four digits only);\nL140@P4: < Dates of birth (use year of birth only);\nL141@P4: < Financial account numbers (identify the type of account and\nL142@P4: institution and provide the last four digits of the account\nL143@P4: number).\nL144@P4: (b) The filer bears sole responsibility for redacting documents.\nL145@P4-5: 5Rule 11 - Other limitations and restrictions concerning Electronic Filing\nL146@P5: (a) Except as otherwise specified in this Rule, or as otherwise ordered, an\nL147@P5: electronic filer duly registered pursuant to Rule 2, above, may only file\nL148@P5: documents in BAP appeals where he or she is counsel of record, or where he\nL149@P5: or she is a party of record appearing pro se.\nL150@P5: (b) Except as otherwise specified in these Rules, or as otherwise ordered, an\nL151@P5: electronic filer may not submit (by US Mail or by fax or by email) additional\nL152@P5: copies of any documents filed electronically through CM/ECF.\nL153@P5: (c) A party seeking to appear as an Amicus Curiae in a BAP appeal should\nL154@P5: contact the BAP Clerk’s Office for guidance if they desire to file\nL155@P5: electronically.\nL156@P5: Rule 12- What is Attached to the Docket available on PACER\nL157@P5: (a) Unless otherwise ordered, all documents that are filed electronically will be\nL158@P5: attached to the PACER docket.\nL159@P5: (b) Unless otherwise ordered, when the BAP receives a document only in paper\nL160@P5: format, the BAP will scan the document and attach it to the PACER docket.\nL161@P5-6: 6SAMPLE CERTIFICATES OF SERVICE\nL162@P6: FOR DOCUMENTS FILED USING CM/ECF\nL163@P6: Certificate of Service When All Case Participants Are CM/ECF Participants\nL164@P6: I hereby certify that on _____[date]______, I electronically filed the foregoing\nL165@P6: document with the Clerk of the Court for the Bankruptcy Appellate Panel for the\nL166@P6: Ninth Circuit by using the CM/ECF system.\nL167@P6: I certify that all parties of record to this appeal either are registered CM/ECF users,\nL168@P6: or have registered for electronic notice, or have consented in writing to electronic\nL169@P6: service, and that service will be accomplished through the CM/ECF system.\nL170@P6: _____________/s/_____________\nL171@P6: ******************************************************************\nL172@P6: Certificate of Service When Not All Case Participants Are CM/ECF\nL173@P6: Participants\nL174@P6: I hereby certify that on _____[date]______, I electronically filed the foregoing\nL175@P6: document with the Clerk of the Court for the Bankruptcy Appellate Panel for the\nL176@P6: Ninth Circuit by using the CM/ECF system.\nL177@P6: I further certify that parties of record to this appeal who either are registered\nL178@P6: CM/ECF users, or who have registered for electronic notice, or who have\nL179@P6: consented in writing to electronic service, will be served through the CM/ECF\nL180@P6: system.\nL181@P6: I further certify that some of the parties of record to this appeal have not consented\nL182@P6: to electronic service. I have mailed the foregoing document by First-Class Mail,\nL183@P6: postage prepaid, or have dispatched it to a third party commercial carrier for\nL184@P6: delivery within 3 calendar days, to the following parties:\nL185@P6: __________________________________________________________________\nL186@P6: __________________________________________________________________\nL187@P6: __________________________________________________________________\nL188@P6: _____________/s/_____________\n"
